--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- DOOM engine: doomgeneric (https://github.com/ozkl/doomgeneric), a portable
  port of id Software's DOOM (https://github.com/id-Software/DOOM), compiled to
  WebAssembly. GPL-2.0.

- The WebAssembly build (engine/doom.js, engine/doom.wasm) and the CommonJS
  engine wrapper are derived from pi-doom (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-doom),
  GPL-2.0.

- Game data: engine/freedoom1.wad is Freedoom Phase 1
  (https://freedoom.github.io/), a free, BSD-3-Clause-licensed Doom-compatible
  IWAD that contains NO id Software assets. © 2001-2024 Contributors to the
  Freedoom project; all rights reserved. Its license text and contributor
  credits are bundled at engine/FREEDOOM-COPYING.txt and
  engine/FREEDOOM-CREDITS.txt, and are reproduced here as required by the
  BSD-3-Clause license.

This project ships NO id Software game assets. DOOM is a trademark of id
Software LLC; Claude and Claude Code are trademarks of Anthropic PBC. This is an
independent, unofficial tool, not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
id Software, ZeniMax, the Freedoom project, or Anthropic. It bundles and
redistributes no Anthropic software — the `split` command only launches the
user's own separately-installed Claude Code alongside the game.
